---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="The Logistics of Large-Scale Import: Shipping $30k+ Orders from China"
  description="Master the logistics of activewear procurement. Learn how to optimize sea and air freight for high-volume orders to minimize landed costs."
>
  <article class="py-32 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 font-['Century_Gothic',sans-serif]">
    <header class="mb-16">
      <span class="text-accent font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">Global Logistics</span>
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-black uppercase tracking-tighter mt-4 mb-8 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">The Logistics of <span class="text-accent italic">Large-Scale Import</span></h2>
      <div class="flex items-center space-x-4 text-gray-500 text-sm">
        <span>Published: June 19, 2026</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>11 Min Read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-xl text-black font-bold mb-8">Shipping is often the single largest variable in your landed cost. For a $30,000 order, the difference between poor and optimal logistics can be $5,000 or more.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-black uppercase mt-12 mb-6 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">1. Sea Freight vs. Air Express</h2>
      <p>For small orders (under 200kg), Air Express is the only viable option. However, once your order reaches the $20k+ range, <strong>LCL (Less than Container Load)</strong> or even a small <strong>20ft FCL (Full Container Load)</strong> becomes a massive profit driver.</p>
      
      <div class="bg-gray-100 p-8 rounded-3xl my-8">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-black mb-4">Landed Cost Comparison (Per Unit):</h4>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
          <li>✈️ <strong>Air Express:</strong> $2.50 - $4.00 per unit (5-7 days)</li>
          <li>🚢 <strong>Sea Freight:</strong> $0.60 - $1.20 per unit (25-35 days)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-black uppercase mt-12 mb-6 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">2. DDP vs. FOB: Which is Better?</h2>
      <p>Many of our high-volume US partners prefer <strong>DDP (Delivered Duty Paid)</strong>. This means Fitclo handles all customs clearance and import duties, delivering directly to your warehouse. This "hands-off" approach is ideal for retailers who want to focus on sales rather than complex customs paperwork.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-black uppercase mt-12 mb-6 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">3. Warehousing and Buffer Stock</h2>
      <p>Large-scale partners often utilize our warehousing capabilities in China. By placing a $50,000 order but shipping it in three $15,000 installments, you lock in volume discounts while managing your warehouse space and cash flow more effectively. We offer free storage for up to 60 days for our premium B2B partners.</p>
    </div>

    <footer class="mt-20 pt-10 border-t border-gray-100">
      <div class="bg-black text-white p-12 rounded-[40px] text-center">
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tighter mb-6">Simplify Your Import</h3>
        <p class="mb-8 text-white/70">Get a comprehensive landed cost analysis for your next major order.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-accent text-black px-10 py-4 rounded-full font-black uppercase tracking-widest hover:scale-105 transition-transform">Get Shipping Quote</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
